  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring &amp; Communicating Results Capacity-Building for the Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot; The objective of the grant is to enhance the capacity of the Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process (OPAPP) to manage, monitor, evaluate and communicate the results of the Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan or PAMANA (&quot;&quot;Program for Resilient Communities in Conflict-Affected Areas or LEGACY) project.  PAMANA is the government&apos;s major new initiative to promote early recovery and build resilient communities in conflict-affected areas, particularly in Mindanao. The grant will support achievement of the Philippines CAS 2010-2012 Strategic Objective 4.3, &quot;&quot;Stability and Peace&quot;&quot;.  In particular it will contribute to Outcome 1 under SO 4.3, &quot;&quot;enhanced impact and conflict-sensitivity of development programs implemented in communities in Mindanao affected by armed or violent conflict.&quot;&quot; This will be achieved by supporting the institutional capacity of OPAPP, as the government&apos;s lead agency for peace and conflict issues, to develop and manage the PAMANA initiative.  The grant will complement significant TA on conflict issues being provided to the government, including OPAPP, under the State and Peace-Building Fund.  It will also support the ongoing development of the Bank&apos;s Mindanao program, as the ARMM Social Fund and the Mindanao Trust Fund (MTF) will be incorporated into the PAMANA umbrella. OPAPP is a key institution for the MTF in particular, as the co-chair of the MTF Interim Steering Committee. manage, monitor, evaluate and communicate the results of the Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan or PAMANA (Program for Resilient&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
